# ScrollBench Test Application - Implementation Complete

## Summary

Successfully created isolated test application **ScrollBench** to validate viewport culling and frame budget optimizations for handling 10,000+ thumbnails without blocking the UI thread.

---

## What Was Built

### C++ Components ✅

1. **[ScrollBenchImageModel](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h)**
   - Viewport culling with [visibleStartIndex](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#37-39)/[visibleEndIndex](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#41-42) properties
   - Generates 10,000 synthetic test items (colored rectangles)
   - Only loads thumbnails for visible range +/- 10 item buffer
   - Tracks pending decode count

2. **[FrameBudgetScheduler](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/FrameBudgetScheduler.h)**
   - Limits texture uploads to configurable amount per frame (default: 10)
   - 16ms frame boundary detection for 60 FPS target
   - Defers excess completions to next frame
   - Prevents UI stuttering during heavy load

3. **[TelemetryMonitor](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/TelemetryMonitor.h)**
   - Real-time FPS tracking (rolling 60-frame average)
   - Memory usage monitoring (Windows PROCESS_MEMORY_COUNTERS)
   - Pending decode queue depth
   - Cache hit rate tracking

